The Fuse ability is used to combine weapons, materials, shields, and more together in The Legend of Zelda: Tears of the Kingdom (TotK). Learn how to fuse and unfuse weapons, the best fused weapons to get, how to unlock the fuse ability, and the fuse ability controls!\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs26 \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 With the Fuse Ability selected, press\'a0
\f1\b L
\f0\b0 . The skill will activate, and objects that can be fused with will glow a jade-green. \
Target the object you want to fuse your weapons with, and press\'a0
\f1\b ZL 
\f0\b0 to fuse it to your equipped shield, or\'a0
\f1\b Y
\f0\b0 \'a0to fuse it to your equipped weapon. \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 Note:\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0Fusing seems to restore some durability. A badly damaged weapon, when fused, will allow it to be used for an extended period.\
With a bow equipped, draw your bow with\'a0
\f1\b ZR. 
\f0\b0 As you are aiming, you can press and hold the\'a0
\f1\b Up
\f0\b0 \'a0button\'a0on the D-Pad to bring up the Materials menu. Scroll through the materials you have with the\'a0
\f1\b Right Stick
\f0\b0 . Once you've selected the material you want to fuse with your arrow, release the\'a0
\f1\b Up
\f0\b0 \'a0button\'a0and the material should fuse with your arrow. \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 Note:\cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 \'a0It appears that you'll have to fuse materials for each arrow that you use. There is no batch fuse feature available.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs43\fsmilli21600 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 Press the\'a0
\f1\b\fs36 Plus (+) Button
\f0\b0\fs43\fsmilli21600 \'a0to open the Inventory menu and navigate to the Weapons tab. Choose the fused weapon that you want to unfuse and select "
\f1\b\fs36 Destroy Fused Material
\f0\b0\fs43\fsmilli21600 ". This reverts the weapon back to its original state and destroys the fused material.\
Note you can obtain the material when unfusing the weapon if the weapon has\'a0{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://game8.co/games/Zelda-Tears-of-the-Kingdom/archives/412524"}}{\fldrslt 
\f1\b\fs36 \cf5 \strokec5 Fuse Recycling passive ability}}. You can disassemble any weapons and shields with fused materials at the Break-a-Part Shop in Tarrey Town. You can avail Pelison's service for\'a0
\f1\b\fs36 20 Rupees
\f0\b0\fs43\fsmilli21600 \'a0and unfuse weapons or shields from the material you attached at them.\
